=== WEB-SOURCE PARITY (web/src/features/dashboard/components/DashboardGrid.tsx) ===
  - useContainerWidth (the sole "data source") → native GeometryReader; no HTTP, no
    store mutation in the view (the parent supplies the dashboard value + the widget
    renderer, exactly like the web `dashboard` prop + getWidgetDef(...).component).
  - GRID_BREAKPOINTS {lg1200,md996,sm768,xs480} / GRID_COLS {4,3,2,1} / ROW_HEIGHT 80 /
    GRID_MARGIN [16,16] (compact [8,8]) → DashboardBreakpoint + DashboardGridMetrics.
  - activeBreakpoint (getBreakpointFromWidth) → DashboardBreakpoint.resolve(width:).
  - isMobileStack (xs) → DashboardBreakpoint.isMobileStack; full-width LazyVStack stack
    with the 12rem (192pt) min height.
  - getWidgetSizeLive → DashboardGridLayoutMath.widgetSize (active bp → lg → default → 1×1).
  - orderedWidgets (mobile xs y/x order, stable, unplaced kept after) → orderedWidgets().
  - absolute desktop grid (ResponsiveGridLayout x/y/w/h) → DashboardGridFlowLayout
    (SwiftUI `Layout`) + DashboardGridPlacement frame math + auto-flow placements().
  - WidgetChrome (drag handle + name + Settings + Remove) → DashboardWidgetChrome.
  - view-mode Expand button → tile expand affordance; FullscreenOverlay (rows≥4) →
    DashboardFullscreenView presented as a cross-platform `.sheet` (iOS + macOS HIG).
  - edit-mode radial-gradient dot pattern (40px) → DashboardDotGridBackground (Canvas).
  - kioskPanelStyle (alpha 0.03+op*0.17, blur 4+op*12) → DashboardKioskStyle.resolve.
  - showWidgetBorders / compactMode / dashboardVehicleId → DashboardGridOptions.
  - SectionErrorBoundary + Suspense(Skeleton) → grid-level loading/error chrome (the
    individual widget bodies own their own load/error state — separate P4 surfaces).
  - web aria-labels (`Settings for ${name}`, `Remove ${name}`, `Expand ${name}`) +
    "Exit Fullscreen" → keyed i18n with %@ interpolation (no hardcoded English).

